🧠 CONCEPTS YOU LEARN FROM THIS CODE
1️⃣ Array Chunking (Very Common Pattern)
What is chunking?

Breaking a big array into smaller arrays of fixed size

Example:

arr = [1,2,3,4,5]
size = 2

Output → [[1,2],[3,4],[5]]


👉 Used in:

Pagination

Batching API calls

Data processing

LeetCode problems

2️⃣ Looping With Custom Step Size (i += size)
This is VERY important
for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i += size)


Instead of:

i++


You jump by size steps.

📌 Meaning:

“Start a new chunk every size elements”

This teaches:

Controlled iteration

Efficient traversal

3️⃣ slice() – Non-Mutating Array Method
arr.slice(start, end)

Key points:

Returns a new array

Does NOT modify original array

end is not included

Example:

[1,2,3,4].slice(1,3) → [2,3]


👉 Interview-friendly:

“slice is safe; splice mutates”

4️⃣ Understanding Half-Open Ranges [i, i+size)
slice(i, i + size)


This teaches a core programming concept:

Start index = i
End index   = i + size (excluded)


This pattern appears in:

Arrays

Strings

DP windows

